Compliance with docs/18
=======================
- ✓ §13.3 founder fields: email, password, first/last name,
  phone (required) — all present.
- ✓ §13.3 organisation fields: legal_name, type (CLINIC
  default), tax_id (NIP 10-digit regex), vat_id_eu (optional).
- ✓ §13.3 address fields: country_code (PL default), region
  (optional), city, postal_code, street_line, building_number,
  unit_number (optional), directions (optional).
- ✓ Idempotency-key bound to React useId — same-tab resubmits
  return the existing org (matches RegisterOrganization field 15
  contract).
- ✓ §6.3 standing notice: subhead carries the "you'll be the
  clinic administrator…" message in both locales.
- ✓ §14.5: zero hard-coded UI strings.
- ✓ §5 R3: log-in CTA cross-origin to app.superwizor.ai.

Known gaps (deferred)
=====================
- Google OAuth path → feature 4 (gated on Firebase Console toggles
  per task #64).
- Live submission untested in-session — same constraint as
  feature 1; feature 8 (Playwright E2E) covers the end-to-end
  against an emulator + httptest stub.
- countryCode dropdown is single-option (PL only). Other
  countries land when we expand internationally; the schema is
  ready (length(2) regex) and the form already accepts any
  ISO-alpha-2 value.
- NIP checksum (mod-11) not validated client-side. Backend
  validates per docs/18 §13.1 ("Backend still validates
  independently; we never trust the client").

